{"availability":"available","full":"sebastian-hanisch/gatv2-demo","name":"gatv2-demo","description":"GATv2: dynamische Aufmerksamkeit auf einer Lager-Suche - interaktive Streamlit-Demo (numpy von Grund auf)","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T12:53:44Z","updated":"2026-10-04T13:21:46Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sebastianhanisch-gatv2-demo.streamlit.app/","topics":["demo","german","graph-neural-networks","machine-learning","python","streamlit"],"demo":"https://sebastianhanisch-gatv2-demo.streamlit.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.185Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.185Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.185Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.185Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Drittes Stück der Graph-Neural-Network-Linie der \"Konzepte\"-Reihe im Portfolio von Sebastian Hanisch – Operations Research und Machine Learning – und Nachfolger von gat-demo (GCN → GraphSAGE, GAT → GATv2, GIN → Graph Transformer; GraphSAGE, GIN und Graph Transformer sind inzwischen gebaut).","Im Vorgänger lernte ein GAT, welche Nachbarn wichtig sind – aber jeder Kunde ordnet seine Nachbarn in derselben Reihenfolge: die Bewertung ist eine Summe aus einem Anteil des Fragenden und einem des Nachbarn (\"statische Aufmerksamkeit\"). GATv2 (Brody/Alon/Yahav 2022) rechnet $a\\cdot\\mathrm{LeakyReLU}(Wl hi + Wr hj)$: die Nichtlinearität steht vor dem Skalarprodukt, die Rangfolge darf vom Fragenden abhängen. Die Demo zeigt das an einer Lager-Suche, die genau das verlangt (jeder Kunde sucht unter seinen Lagern das mit seinem Artikelcode), und misst ehrlich, was es im Liefergebiet bei falschen…","Bezug zu OR: Zuordnungen wie \"welches Lager bedient diesen Artikel\" hängen vom Artikel ab – ein Modell, das Lager unabhängig von der Anfrage bewertet, kann das nicht abbilden."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/gatv2-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ae1194eb0d88fe1c93426426ca2558268e8274afd81106c1217b01de3421fd91","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.354Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.354Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Drittes Stück der Graph-Neural-Network-Linie der \"Konzepte\"-Reihe im Portfolio von Sebastian Hanisch – Operations Research und Machine Learning – und Nachfolger von gat-demo (GCN → GraphSAGE, GAT → GATv2, GIN → Graph Transformer; GraphSAGE, GIN und Graph Transformer sind inzwischen gebaut).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/gatv2-demo/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"ae1194eb0d88fe1c93426426ca2558268e8274afd81106c1217b01de3421fd91","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/gatv2-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.354Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T13:21:46Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/gatv2-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.355Z","hash":"ae1194eb0d88fe1c93426426ca2558268e8274afd81106c1217b01de3421fd91","originalBytes":11819,"storedBytes":11819,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["die","gatv2","gat","der","und","lager","mit","nicht","ein","gcn","bei","ist","test","kunden","pfe","aufmerksamkeit","das","dem","seed","kunde","kanten","lagern","nur","seeds","von","auch","auf","ber","den","graph","lager-suche","mehr","sind","acht","als","fragenden","liefergebiet","rangfolge","vom","wie","anfrage","aus","beim","des","drei","gegen","kopf","liegt","nachbarn","oder","raten","suche","transformer","zwei","abh","attention","code","depots","dichte","experimente","falschen","gen","graphsage","gro","heads","hinter","jeder","lernen","pfen","punkte","sich","sie","vehikel","warum","anteil","bekannten","cdot","demo","eine","einen","experiment","gin","gradienten","hand","interventionstest","kantenlisten","kein","lle","mittel","mlp"